{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a capture card goes from plugged in to on screen."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePipeline","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HeadwireCapture"}],"title":"The capture pipeline","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call into the capture session runs on one serial queue, owned by an actor whose executor is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that queue, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"startRunning"},{"text":", which blocks until frames flow, never runs on the main thread. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app drives it through ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient","isActive":true},{"text":"; this article follows one card through that client’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"endpoints.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Finding-the-card","text":"Finding the card","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/devices","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" streams the connected external video devices. It observes the discovery","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"session’s device list, which the system updates on every plug and unplug, so there is no polling","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and no fixed delay; repeated lists are dropped. A card can show up before its format list is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"filled in, so ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/start","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" polls for the formats, every 250 ms for up to about two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"seconds, and goes on as soon as they appear."}]},{"text":"Choosing the format","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Choosing-the-format"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/formats"},{"type":"text","text":" returns the formats a device offers, in the order it lists them. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first time the app opens a card, before it sets a format, it records the card’s own active format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and frame duration as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CardPreferredMode"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/start"},{"type":"text","text":" then resolves the format with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"FormatSelection.resolve(_:in:cardPrefers:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the person’s selection where the card offers it,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"else the preferred format, which tries the card’s own mode first and otherwise favours frame rate,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at least 1080p, uncompressed over compressed, and 16:9. The same resolver tells Settings which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format Automatic picked, so the sheet and the stream agree."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session uses the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".inputPriority"},{"type":"text","text":" preset, so the device’s active format is the one applied."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The minimum and maximum frame durations are both pinned to the rate’s exact duration, 1001\/60000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for 59.94 fps, rather than one computed from a rounded rate."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Reading-the-frames","level":3,"text":"Reading the frames"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The session has one video data output, beside the preview layer rather than in front of it. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hands each frame in turn to three consumers: the Metal presenter, the content sampler, and the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"calibration recorder. Uncompressed formats arrive as the card sends them, with nothing converted."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For a codec, the output asks the system to decode, preferring biplanar 4:2:0; where the output"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"offers no uncompressed format, the app decodes Motion JPEG, H.264, or HEVC itself. Late frames are"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"discarded rather than queued.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The content sampler reads one frame on each format change and then one every two seconds, on a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"queue of its own. Each read finds where the Mac’s picture sits inside a padded frame","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/contentBounds"},{"text":"), whether the frames carry the range their pixel format claims","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/rangeReadings"},{"text":"), and what the frame looks like (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/frameLooks","isActive":true},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which the app uses to tell a live picture from a no-signal field. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/recordCalibration","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copies a small crop of every frame for the length of one calibration.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The output also counts the frames that arrive. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/deliveredFrameRate"},{"text":" reports the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rate over the last second. When two meter windows in a row deliver under 90% of the rate the card","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"was set to, and the format was chosen automatically, the session restarts once on another pixel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format at the same resolution and rate, skipping a format that differs only in colour range. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format the person chose in Settings is kept.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Drawing the picture","anchor":"Drawing-the-picture","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePreviewView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" shows the stream. With upscaling off, the session’s own preview layer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"draws it and no frame passes through the app. The Metal path takes over for an upscaler (MetalFX,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or super resolution finished with MetalFX), for a colour correction the card’s profile calls for,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and for a codec the app decodes. It converts each frame on the GPU the moment it arrives and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"presents it straight away, with no display link. If the GPU stages cannot be built, or a frame"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrives in a layout the shader cannot read, the view falls back to the preview layer."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/FrameFeed"},{"type":"text","text":" puts frames from outside a capture session, such as a decoded network stream,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the same Metal path, so scaling, the reported layout, and upscaling behave as they do for"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a card.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"When the session stops","anchor":"When-the-session-stops","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Session notifications are reduced to one ordered stream of events. An interruption is reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CaptureSessionState.interrupted(device:reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and its end as running again. A runtime error"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or the card being unplugged tears the session down and reports a failure. After a media services"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reset the session restarts the last request from scratch, up to three times a minute; past that it","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails and the person is asked to replug the card."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/capturepipeline"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/start":{"title":"start","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/start","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"start"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"device"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel0B6DeviceV","text":"CaptureDevice"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel0B6DeviceV2IDa","text":"ID"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"selection"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel15FormatSelectionV","text":"FormatSelection"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida","text":"Void"}],"deprecated":true,"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/start","abstract":[{"text":"Streams a device, using the selection when the device supports it and its preferred format otherwise.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/contentBounds":{"url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/contentbounds","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the source’s picture sits inside the padded frame, emitted now and again on every change."}],"title":"contentBounds","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"contentBounds","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"ContentBounds","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel13ContentBoundsV"},{"text":"?>","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/contentBounds"},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/frameLooks":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/frameLooks","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/framelooks","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The look of each frame the content sampler reads, about every two seconds while frames flow."}],"title":"frameLooks","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"frameLooks"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" () -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","text":"AsyncStream"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel9FrameLookV","text":"FrameLook"},{"kind":"text","text":"?>"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture","role":"collection","title":"HeadwireCapture","type":"topic","abstra